{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Aluf Korah.</b> The one mentioned among the sons of Eliphaz — one may say that it is Timna among the sons of Eliphaz, mentioned in Chronicles, for among the sons of Oholivamah there is another Korah. And in tractate Sotah, Rashi explained: there is Korah son of Eliphaz and there is Korah son of Oholivamah. And one may say that both are one and the same, and the reason Scripture mentioned him among the chieftains of Eliphaz is that he dwelt with them, and Oholivamah his mother died while he was still young, and Adah took him and raised him with her children, and he lived and was to her as a son. And so we find that Amalek is recorded among the sons of Adah, because he was the son of her son's maidservant."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {0 "The phrase י״‎מ ('one may say') introduces the suggestion that Korah is to be identified with Timna; the logic is that Timna is listed among Eliphaz's sons in Chronicles, and since a separate Korah appears among Oholivamah's sons, the Korah in Eliphaz's list may be explained through Timna's connection to Eliphaz's household."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:07:32.854864352Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}